    <title>Daily Digest 2026-08-28: Kubernetes v1.37: Metrics API graduates to stable; Building an AI factory on Kubernetes; Making Your Data Ready for Agentic AI</title>
    <updated>2026-08-28T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://islandirie.github.io/my-rss-feed/daily/2026-08-28.html"/>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Kubernetes v1.37: Metrics API graduates to stable&lt;/b&gt; — Kubernetes ecosystem changes can surface new operational patterns or affect your existing clusters. &lt;a href="https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/27/kubernetes-v1-37-metrics-api-ga/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Building an AI factory on Kubernetes&lt;/b&gt; — Kubernetes ecosystem changes can surface new operational patterns or affect your existing clusters. &lt;a href="https://www.cncf.io/blog/2026/08/27/building-an-ai-factory-on-kubernetes/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Making Your Data Ready for Agentic AI&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://martinfowler.com/articles/making-data-ready-for-agentic-ai.html"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;When you keep AI Lean, you keep AI correct&lt;/b&gt; — Flagged as relevant to your interests — read the summary to decide if it's worth your time. &lt;a href="https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/08/28/when-you-keep-ai-lean-you-keep-ai-correct/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Breaking Claude Code Opus 5 Auto Mode&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/27/breaking-claude-code-opus-5-auto-mode/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Two Alleged ‘TeamPCP’ Hackers Arrested in Australia&lt;/b&gt; — Supply chain risks are often overlooked until it's too late — track these proactively. &lt;a href="https://krebsonsecurity.com/2026/08/two-alleged-teampcp-hackers-arrested-in-australia/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Beckon, distinct sounds for what your AI coding agent needs&lt;/b&gt; — Community-vetted signal from Hacker News — high upvote-to-age ratio means the engineering community found it worth reading. &lt;a href="https://github.com/Isa1asN/beckon"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Rafter – an MCP server that shares one team's memory, skills and agents&lt;/b&gt; — Expanding what LLMs can interact with — relevant if you're building or using agentic pipelines. &lt;a href="https://heyrafter.xyz/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Puppetflow a free browser automation platform&lt;/b&gt; — Better visibility into your systems — new tooling or standards that reduce MTTR. &lt;a href="https://github.com/puppetflow/puppetflow"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supporting Thailand’s next generation of AI startups&lt;/b&gt; — Flagged as relevant to your interests — read the summary to decide if it's worth your time. &lt;a href="https://openai.com/index/supporting-next-generation-ai-startups-thailand"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
